    "knowledge_point": "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval: Lower Bound is Not Zero",
    "problem": "Given that $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.23),$ compute $P(3<X<7)$ rounded to $4$ decimal places.",
    "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.23),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(0.77)}^{x-1}(0.23), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<X<7) & =P(X\\in \\{4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=4)+P(X=5)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =f(4)+f(5)+f(6) \\\\  & ={(0.77)}^{3}(0.23)+{(0.77)}^{4}(0.23)+{(0.77)}^{5}(0.23) \\\\  & ≈0.2481.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
